      "text": "Concentration of Measure Techniques and Applications — 36 sections: Front matter; Biographical Sketch; Acknowledgments\n\n**Concentration of Measure Techniques and Applications**\n\n*Meg Walters*\n\n134 pp, 36 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Biographical Sketch; Acknowledgments; Abstract; Contributors and Funding Sources; List of Figures; 1 Introduction; 2 Concentration of Measure Results and other N; 2.1 Talagrand's Gaussian Concentration of Meas; 2.2 Talagrand's Isoperimetric Inequality; 2.3 Ledoux's Concentration of Measure on Rever; 2.4 The Euler-Maclaurin Formula; 3 Random Operator Compressions; 3.1 Background for First Result; 3.2 Kac's Walk on SO(n); 3.3 Main Result; 3.4 Kac's Model Coupled to a Thermostat; 3.5 An Additional Application: The Length of t",
